  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Isoko y&apos;Ubuzima</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Rwanda):  ...Isoko y&apos;Ubuzima (Source of life in Kinyarwanda) will contribute to the Government of Rwanda (GOR)&apos;s target of reaching 100% of all Rwandans with improved access to basic water and sanitation services by 2024 and achieving the Sustainable Development Goal 6 to ensure access to water and sanitation for all by 2030... ..The activity aims to improve access to and utilization of safe, sustainable drinking water and sanitation services. These interventions are expected to increase access to water supply services for 120,000 people (approximately 24,000 households); increase access to improved sanitation and hygiene services for 100,000 people (20,000 households); increase by 19 percent, the number of households with soap and water at a handwashing station; and improve water supply services for 96,000 people. $1,100,000 of funding within this activity contributes to meeting the required &quot;safe latrines&quot; earmark of $1,100,000. .. ..The activity will assist the Government of Rwanda to address the challenges identified in 2022 WASH sector performance assessment and align with MININFRA&apos;s multi-year action plan. In addition, the activity will rehabilitate a total of 16 non-functioning Water Supply systems (WSS) in 10 targeted districts during which 40,000 people will gain access to drinking water and 20,000 will benefit from improved services... ..WASH programs contribute to a range of human development outcomes, including promoting livelihoods, reducing child mortality and infectious diseases, reducing student absenteeism, mitigating conflict, empowering women and girls, and enhancing government effectiveness through improved service provision. By improving access to and utilization of WASH services and products, this activity will contribute to the Health Development Objective of improved health outcomes in the Mission&apos;s CDCS 2020 - 2025.........</narrative>
  </description>
